    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "I was on the fence about touching it, but I'm now leaning on updating this.\r\n\r\nMy reason for leaving it was that returning the range for the unrefined value is technically incorrect. It also would require a different logic in all range input components to display an empty string when `value === range`.\r\n\r\nBut, I'm starting to think it might be better to let users return an empty string, instead of having them reimplement this more complicated check.\r\n\r\nI'll update the behavior.",
    "commit_id": "c5f05da9ae9cefb41fb8388b27ba3d30be4bfa51",
    "created_at": "2025-01-06T13:45:48Z",
    "diff_hunk": "@@ -144,15 +144,19 @@ const renderer =\n     }\n \n     const { min: rangeMin, max: rangeMax } = range;\n-    const [minValue, maxValue] = start;\n+    const { min: minValue, max: maxValue } = currentRefinement;\n \n     const step = 1 / Math.pow(10, widgetParams.precision || 0);\n \n     const values = {\n       min:\n-        minValue !== -Infinity && minValue !== rangeMin ? minValue : undefined,\n+        typeof minValue === 'number' && minValue !== rangeMin\n+          ? minValue\n+          : undefined,\n       max:\n-        maxValue !== Infinity && maxValue !== rangeMax ? maxValue : undefined,\n+        typeof maxValue === 'number' && maxValue !== rangeMax",
